##
# TabDock .gitattributes
# Repository: TabDock (.NET 8 / WPF / C# 12, Windows desktop utility)
#
# Line-ending policy. The working tree intentionally mixes CRLF sources
# (C#/XAML/MSBuild files expected by Visual Studio and the WPF toolchain)
# and LF files (docs, PowerShell scripts, YAML/JSON). `* text=auto` keeps
# every text file normalized to LF in the repository; the per-type `eol=`
# rules below pin checkout line endings so they are stable regardless of a
# developer's `core.autocrlf` setting.
#
# NOTE: after this file lands, the maintainer must run a one-time
# `git add --renormalize .` to rewrite the index with these attributes.
# (Agents must not run git commands - this is a manual, one-time step.)
##

* text=auto

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CRLF on checkout: Windows-native toolchain sources
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.cs     text eol=crlf
*.xaml   text eol=crlf
*.csproj text eol=crlf
*.sln    text eol=crlf

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# LF on checkout: docs, scripts, and config
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.md    text eol=lf
*.ps1   text eol=lf
*.yaml  text eol=lf
*.yml   text eol=lf
*.json  text eol=lf

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Binary assets: never normalized, never diffed as text
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.bmp  binary
*.ico  binary
*.pdf  binary
